# SPEC: 65_symbol_clearance
# Requires: driver
# static-check: off
# NEEDS: write
# REPLACE-LEVEL: 3
# NEGATIVE (spec/65 F65-32): the environment is the PROCESS default and may only
# TIGHTEN.  The host sets `AIML_REPLACE_LEVEL=3`; the call demands 7 — and gets 3.
#
# Here "stricter" runs in the OTHER direction than for the clearance, because the comparison
# is reversed (`clearance <= replace_level`): stricter is the SMALLER number.  Exactly
# that is why "not set" is not 0 but "no default" — if it were 0, the
# environment could only switch the right off and never grant it.
#
# Difference from n22: there the right IS granted and the version carries the statement
# (`clearance-collision`).  Here the right is capped by the environment, so it never gets
# as far as the version — the check order from F65-29 becomes visible here once more.
#
# The rule has TWO directions, and this probe covers only one.  The other was measured on 2026-10-17,
# because one probe alone cannot tell "capped" from "call ignored"
# apart:
#   AIML_REPLACE_LEVEL=7 + call 0 → effectively 0, clearance-replace  (the call tightens)
#   AIML_REPLACE_LEVEL=7 + call 7 → granted, then clearance-collision (n22 file)
# So the stricter one always wins, from whichever source it comes.
# EXPECT-ERROR: clearance-replace
- def:
    name: wipe_queue
    return: i32
    body:
      - return: [0]

- def:
    name: main
    return: i32
    body:
      - decl: [pkg, Code, { call: [sys.bundle, "wipe_queue", { context: false }] }]
      - decl: [rcx, i32, { call: [sys.exec, pkg, 7, 7, 7] }]
      - return: [rcx]
